 "comments": [
  {
   "rating": 44,
   "date": "2006-08-17T09:03:25-05:00",
   "body": "Another great way to approach this is to get the 'Find Bingles' quest from Gnoarm at IF. Once you find Bingles (East coast of Loch Modan at coords 63,48), you go out to the Northernmost islands to get his tools. There are plenty of Seers and Skullthumpers on that island that you will need to go through to get to the tools, so you can complete both quests at once (they are in groups, so bring a friend or two).\nHope this helps.",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 13,
   "date": "2006-08-17T09:03:25-05:00",
   "body": "The Skullthumpers and the Seers are in both places mentioned above: They're behind the troggs on the hill in Stonesplinter Valley (near the caves on your map) at [b]36,80[/b]. They can also be found on the northern most island in The Loch which is northeast of Thelsamar (you must swim to get there) at [b]50,25[/b].",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 5,
   "date": "2007-05-09T05:53:42-05:00",
   "body": "You can find them up a hill around 34.78",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 1,
   "date": "2006-07-11T21:03:25-05:00",
   "body": "they are at 36,80 on top of hill in stonesplinter valley",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 1,
   "date": "2006-08-17T09:03:25-05:00",
   "body": "yeah you have to go through the camp where the troggs are",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 1,
   "date": "2006-06-18T13:52:40-05:00",
   "body": "You could do this quest while collecting Bingle's Tools on the trogg island in the north end of the Loch.  2 of the tools are surrounded by these 2 types.",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 1,
   "date": "2007-01-31T21:35:06-06:00",
   "body": "Same here MissusLewis, seemed really random.",
   "replies": []
  },
  {
   "rating": 1,
   "date": "2006-05-21T20:36:29-05:00",
   "body": "Don't get it twisted...those coords are DEAD ON. But you have to get through a big Trogg camp to get to them. This isn't just a stroll to the coords. If you are lucky you can kill off the peripheral troggs and sneak thru the middle of the 4 camps in the area to the pathway you need to get to. Once there, then you can pick these off 1 by 1.  But I was shocked to find this HUGE camp of Troggs in the area, especially cuz I never noticed the pathway off the main road before.",
   "replies": []
  },
